From: Maximilian Gaedig <sly-keg-cheating@duck.com>
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: qcom: sdm845: use CXO_CLK_A for remoteproc xo

clk-rpmh gives the plain rpmhcc XO a valid_state_mask of
WAKE | ACTIVE | SLEEP, while the _A variant votes in WAKE | ACTIVE only.
An AP-side reference on the plain clock therefore writes xo.lvl = 0x3
("on") into the RPMH *sleep* set, keeping the 19.2 MHz crystal running
while the AP is asleep. AOSS only reaches its deep states with XO
released, so this pins qcom_stats aosd AND cxsd at 0 together.

All four remoteprocs took the plain clock as their "xo", so merely having
the DSPs loaded was enough to hold it. Each DSP has its own RSC and votes
XO for itself while running -- the AP does not need to hold it on their
behalf across AP sleep.

Measured on a OnePlus 6, fully quiesced with cx/mx/cx_ao all off-0 and the
cx.lvl sleep vote correctly written as 0, the sleep set still contained
xo.lvl = 0x3. After this change bi_tcxo's enable count drops from 302 to
45 and its consumers are UFS and the USB PHYs; all four remoteprocs move
to bi_tcxo_ao.

Note this alone does not clear xo.lvl: UFS (ref_clk) and the USB PHYs
still hold the plain clock, so the sleep vote remains 0x3 on a system
whose UFS is up and whose USB cable is attached.

Signed-off-by: Maximilian Gaedig <sly-keg-cheating@duck.com>
---
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sdm845.dtsi	2026-09-02 22:36:29.285212714 +0200
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sdm845.dtsi	2026-09-02 22:36:29.317516391 +0200
@@ -910,7 +910,23 @@
 		interrupt-names = "wdog", "fatal", "ready",
 				  "handover", "stop-ack";
 
-		clocks = <&rpmhcc RPMH_CXO_CLK>;
+		/*
+		 * CXO_CLK_A, not CXO_CLK. The plain rpmhcc XO has
+		 * valid_state_mask = WAKE | ACTIVE | SLEEP, so an AP-side
+		 * reference on it writes xo.lvl = 0x3 ("on") into the RPMH
+		 * *sleep* set. Merely having the remoteprocs loaded therefore
+		 * kept the 19.2 MHz crystal voted on while the AP slept, and
+		 * AOSS can only reach its deep states with XO released -- so
+		 * qcom_stats aosd AND cxsd both stayed pinned at 0, together,
+		 * even with cx/mx/cx_ao all off-0 and the cx.lvl sleep vote
+		 * correctly written as 0.
+		 *
+		 * The _A variant votes in WAKE | ACTIVE only. Each DSP has its
+		 * own RSC and votes XO for itself while it is running, so the
+		 * AP does not need to hold it on the DSP's behalf across AP
+		 * sleep.
+		 */
+		clocks = <&rpmhcc RPMH_CXO_CLK_A>;
 		clock-names = "xo";
 
 		memory-region = <&adsp_mem>;
@@ -1046,7 +1062,7 @@
 		interrupt-names = "wdog", "fatal", "ready",
 				  "handover", "stop-ack";
 
-		clocks = <&rpmhcc RPMH_CXO_CLK>;
+		clocks = <&rpmhcc RPMH_CXO_CLK_A>;
 		clock-names = "xo";
 
 		memory-region = <&cdsp_mem>;
@@ -3454,7 +3470,7 @@
 				 <&gcc GCC_MSS_SNOC_AXI_CLK>,
 				 <&gcc GCC_MSS_MFAB_AXIS_CLK>,
 				 <&gcc GCC_PRNG_AHB_CLK>,
-				 <&rpmhcc RPMH_CXO_CLK>;
+				 <&rpmhcc RPMH_CXO_CLK_A>;
 			clock-names = "iface", "bus", "mem", "gpll0_mss",
 				      "snoc_axi", "mnoc_axi", "prng", "xo";
 
@@ -3522,7 +3538,7 @@
 			interrupt-names = "wdog", "fatal", "ready",
 						"handover", "stop-ack";
 
-			clocks = <&rpmhcc RPMH_CXO_CLK>;
+			clocks = <&rpmhcc RPMH_CXO_CLK_A>;
 			clock-names = "xo";
 
 			qcom,qmp = <&aoss_qmp>;
